PW water dimer, two molecules stacked 7.5 bohr apart along z, with native SCCS in a periodic
cell (assume_isolated none), the water-neutral preset and the Environ solvent-aware interface
(sccs_solvent_radius 2, sccs_filling_threshold 0.3). The probe of radius 4 bohr fills the gap
between the molecules but not the gaps to the periodic images: Environ 'chain' derivatives of
the filled boundary, the probe adjoint in the electronic potential, energy and ionic force.

Reference provenance (ecutwfc 75 Ry / ecutrho 300 Ry, the cutoffs of the QE-Environ comparison):
- ABACUS source commit: 4136a53bf (feat(input): add the SCCS solvent-aware INPUT keys)
- ABACUS version: v3.11.0-beta10
- executable SHA256: 9c6f666ca6e025e4dd41dc936bfe056aee0b74f4997053ebfeed6355868d72d6
- parallel layout: 16 MPI ranks x 1 OpenMP thread
- generated 2026-09-29; two independent check runs passed every comparison.
- sccs_debug 2 reports SCCS_CAVITY FILLED_VOLUME/Bohr3 104.7 at convergence.
- result.ref is an ABACUS regression baseline, not an external QE/Environ reference; the
  solvent-aware kernel was compared with QE-Environ 3.1.1 on Environ's own solvent-aware test
  system (see the PR description).

Repository harness regeneration command, run from tests/01_PW:
  OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 bash ../integrate/Autotest.sh -a /path/to/abacus -n 16 -o 1 -r '^220_PW_SCCS_SA_PERIODIC_WATER2$' -g
